test.yaml:16:14: "aube install" runs the lifecycle scripts of every dependency (`--dangerously-allow-all-builds`), and a compromised release uses them to run code on the runner. aube runs only the scripts that `allowBuilds` and its built-in list of trusted packages allow: remove this, review what was skipped with `aube ignored-builds` and approve the packages that need a build with `aube approve-builds` [unlocked-install]
