test.yaml:34:14: "aube install" runs the lifecycle scripts of every dependency (an earlier script sets `dangerouslyAllowAllBuilds`), and a compromised release uses them to run code on the runner. aube runs only the scripts that `allowBuilds` and its built-in list of trusted packages allow: remove this, review what was skipped with `aube ignored-builds` and approve the packages that need a build with `aube approve-builds` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:41:14: "aube add" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. aube waits one day for a release by default (`minimumReleaseAge` of 1440 minutes), but the settings of this install turn that off. set `minimumReleaseAge` (in minutes) to more than 0 in aube-workspace.yaml, or remove the setting that makes it 0 [unlocked-install]
